cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DanaFish: automated detection and counting of dorsal root ganglion neurons in zebrafish"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bakhshi
    given-names: Mostafa
repository-code: "https://github.com/mostafabakhshi/DanaFish"
abstract: >-
  DanaFish is an image-analysis pipeline for counting dorsal root ganglion (DRG)
  neuronal cell bodies in fluorescence images of zebrafish larvae. It corrects the
  background pedestal, standardizes larval orientation with a YOLO26m landmark
  detector, detects neurons with a YOLO26m detector, restricts counting to the
  spinal-cord region, and exports counts with their somite-level positions. It runs
  fully automatically over a folder of images, or in a semi-automatic mode in which
  the automatic result is presented for expert correction.
keywords:
  - zebrafish
  - dorsal root ganglion
  - neuron counting
  - object detection
  - YOLO
  - bioimage analysis
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-15"
